街区レベル位置参照情報 国土交通省 (MLIT, Ministry of Land, Infrastructure, Transport and Tourism,
Japan), 2025年度版, version 24.0a: the 47 prefectural archives (01000-24.0a.zip through
47000-24.0a.zip), captured 2026-10-31. Source: https://nlftp.mlit.go.jp/isj/.
Their URLs, byte sizes and SHA-256 checksums are recorded in tests/registry/jp.sources.tsv.

The corpus tests/registry/jp.jsonl was sampled and reformatted by OpenGeocoding from this source.
It decodes Shift-JIS to UTF-8, keeps current representative residential-address blocks with
numeric block signs, transforms JGD2000 geographic coordinates to WGS84, draws a seeded sample,
and constructs query forms from the source's names and block signs. These edits and queries are
not unmodified MLIT publications and are not endorsed by MLIT. Points represent blocks, not
individual residences or entrances.

Used under the 位置参照情報利用約款 (Location Reference Information Terms of Use, revised
2013-02-07), https://nlftp.mlit.go.jp/isj/agreement.html: free use, including reproduction,
citation and edited outputs, with the required source credit above and, where possible, edition,
filename and the party responsible for the edits. The information is not suitable for surveys
requiring high accuracy or official certifications; use is at the user's responsibility.
MLIT disclaims liability and may change the terms or withdraw the service.

デジタル庁 アドレス・ベース・レジストリ (Digital Agency, Address Base Registry),
https://www.digital.go.jp/policies/base_registry_address, used under Creative Commons
Attribution 4.0 International (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/), as permitted by
PDL1.0 and the dataset-specific terms:
https://www.digital.go.jp/policies/base_registry_address_tos.

The separate tests/registry/jp.abr.jsonl corpus uses residence-level records from the
OpenAddresses export jp_abr_residential.csv.zip, uploaded 2026-10-01:
https://data.openaddresses.io/cache/uploads/jeffdefacto/2026-10-01-tkes5/jp_abr_residential.csv.zip.
OpenAddresses joined ABR's residence master, residence-position extension, town and city
masters using scripts/jp/abr_residential.py at commit 5172acb847e0127cab772a75f92b43444cac5db0.
The export is not geocoder output. It drops per-record CRS, scale and coordinate-source codes
and chooses one of multiple position records for the same residence. Underlying data remains
experimental outside the formally maintained town-name text, with no freshness guarantee.

OpenGeocoding samples eligible residences, constructs two native-script country-qualified
query forms, adds postcode punctuation, rounds source coordinates to six decimals and uses
JGD2011 geographic coordinates as WGS84 at a 150 m diagnostic tolerance. These edits are not
unmodified publications of the Digital Agency or OpenAddresses and imply no endorsement.
The corpus is not a survey or certification of individual entrances or national accuracy.
The ABR export also supplies index data, so agreement is source consistency, not independent
real-world accuracy. No ABR residence data was added to the index by this corpus change.
